<title>UK: LucasVarity to announce job cuts - paper.</title>
<headline>LucasVarity to announce job cuts - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-American automotive and aerospace components group LucasVarity Plc is expected on Tuesday to announce a fundamental restructuring of its manufacturing operations in a shake-up that could lead to several thousand job losses, the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>The company, which was formed earlier this year through the 3.2 billion stg merger of Lucas Industries and Varity Corp of the U.S., is planning to accelerate it 115 million stg cost savings programme, the FT said.</p>
<p>Closing plants and reducing areas of overlap could save the enlarged company more than 200 million stg over the next two years, the FT said.</p>
<p>In September, LucasVarity told Reuters around 450 jobs would go in the combined group which employs 56,000 workers. But the company declined to say whether more job losses were on the cards.</p>
